Porto quiet Windows tool-directory PATH update for Lima v2.3.0 (Apache-2.0).

Lima 2.3.0 logs at Info level, before its flags are parsed, whenever it appends
an existing QEMU or MSYS2 directory to PATH on Windows. Every limactl call then
writes that line to stderr, so it appears in container output streamed through
`limactl shell` and in diagnostics Porto parses. Keep the PATH update and log
it at Debug level instead.

diff --git a/cmd/limactl/main.go b/cmd/limactl/main.go
index 6ed4da7..836ae44 100644
--- a/cmd/limactl/main.go
+++ b/cmd/limactl/main.go
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ func main() {
 		p := os.Getenv("PATH")
 		newPath := envutil.AppendDirsToPath(p, envutil.PlatformCommonToolDirs)
 		if newPath != p {
-			logrus.Info("Temporarily add the common tool (QEMU etc.) directories to PATH")
+			logrus.Debug("Temporarily add the common tool (QEMU etc.) directories to PATH")
 			if err := os.Setenv("PATH", newPath); err != nil {
 				logrus.WithError(err).Warning("Can't add common tool directories to PATH, relying entirely on system PATH")
 			}
